Third-party MCP servers
=======================

Some entries in this catalog package MCP servers written by others. SOCIS
writes the manifest — the entry name, description, credential prompts and
install experience — but the server itself is upstream code.

MIT states one condition and it is this:

    The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included
    in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

So attribution is not optional, and removing it would turn a compliant use
into an infringement. It also has a practical purpose: without a recorded
upstream repository, .github/workflows/upstream-watch.yml cannot tell us when
one of these servers ships a security fix, and we would be shipping
unmaintained code into customer SOCs without knowing.


