Modifications made by SOCIS
---------------------------
None to the server code. SOCIS supplies only the catalog manifest: entry name,
description, credential declarations, suggestion triggers and post-install
guidance. Entries are named for the capability an analyst gets rather than for
the upstream project, which is a packaging choice and not a claim of
authorship.


Review status
-------------
These servers are pinned and packaged as-is. They have NOT been line-by-line
audited by SOCIS beyond the review recorded in
optional-mcps/MCP-IMPLEMENTATION-TRACKING.md.

This matters more than it would for a skill. A skill is markdown that a human
reads; an MCP server is executable code holding credentials to a customer's
security platform. Review any entry before enabling it in a client
environment, and note in particular that endpoint-siem exposes Wazuh
active-response tooling capable of isolating hosts and killing processes.


